TITLE: COMMENTARY has no per-type narrative
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Every grammar type except COMMENTARY has a NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-TYPE-* narrative
in docs/spec/ carrying TAGS: <TYPE> and a first-sentence gloss; COMMENTARY has
none, so a Grammars tab that renders type cards from those narratives (the
generate-not-hard-code direction under discussion 2026-09-02) would have no
gloss for it and a narrative-driven coverage check would flag it. Found while
copying the glosses into grammar-groups.json (b6c01bd4).
<<<
